    "title": "South Dakota District 17: One drops out of race, another enters - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Reilly Mahon Maren Ewertz ,\n1 hours ago\nSOUTH DAKOTA ( KCAU ) — A couple of changes are coming to some of the southeastern South Dakota races.\nWilliam Shorma withdrew his name from the District 17 race; he will no longer run for re-election. Shorma has held that seat since 2022.\nInstead, Shorma is running as a Republican for the District 1 seat on the Union County Commission.\nRELATED: Who is on the ballot for South Dakota’s 2026 primaries? Meanwhile, Troy Redler is running as a Republican for the District 17 seat. The business owner said that being accessible and transparent will be priorities if he is elected.\nA total of three GOP ( Chris Kassin , Troy Redler , and Robin Schiro) and two Democratic ( Austin Brunick and Leslie Gerrish ) candidates are vying for the two District 17 seats.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KCAU 9 News | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
    "summary": "William Shorma withdrew his name from the District 17 race; he will no longer run for re-election. Instead, Shorma is running as a Republican for the District 1 seat on the Union County Commission. Meanwhile, Troy Redler is running as a Republican for the District 17 seat. The business owner said that being accessible and transparent will be priorities if he is elected. A total of three GOP ( Chris Kassin , Troy Redler , and Robin Schiro) and two Democratic ( Austin Brunick and Leslie Gerrish ) candidates are vying for the two District 17 seats.",
